.\" man/man3/TreeSitter::Detector.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "TreeSitter::Detector" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "treesitter 0.1.0" "treesitter API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
TreeSitter::Detector \- Guesses the language of source text that has no file name, such as a snippet.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "treesitter/detect"\fR
.sp
\fBclass TreeSitter::Detector\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Guesses the language of source text that has no file name, such as a snippet. A calibrated \fB\%RLCD::Model\fR trained
on code samples ranks the languages; labels are grammar names for \fB\%Language.find\fR. Optionally (\fB\%checked\fR > 0) the
grammars of the most probable ones parse the text, and candidates whose parse has errors lose probability to
those that parse cleanly. A detector reuses one \fB\%Parser\fR, so it is not safe to share between threads.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.default : Detector\fR
The bundled detector, built by \fB\%scripts/model.cr\fR from the test corpora and examples of the Tier 1 grammars;
\fB\%models/REPORT.md\fR lists its languages and measured accuracy. Each call returns a new detector, so each fiber
can hold its own.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.load(path : String) : Detector\fR
Loads a detector saved with \fB\%save\fR, JSON or binary (detected from the content); raises \fB\%RLCD::FormatError\fR for a
malformed file.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.new(model : RLCD::Model, checked : Int32 = 0, penalty : Float64 = 1.0, threshold : Float64 = 0.5, timeout : Time::Span = 50.milliseconds)\fR
A detector over \fImodel\fR, whose labels are grammar names.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.train(samples : Hash(String, Array(String)), *, dim : Int32 = 4096, seed : UInt64 = 42_u64, hidden : Int32 = 0, epochs : Int32 = 60, lr : Float64 = 0.01, validation : Float64 = 0.15, calibration : Hash(String, Array(String)) | Nil = nil, checkpoint : String | Nil = nil, rng : Random = Random.new) : Detector\fR
Trains a detector on \fIsamples\fR: grammar name \[u2192] code snippets, for at least two languages with a snippet each.
Snippets hash into \fIdim\fR code features with \fIseed\fR, which also fixes each epoch\(aqs shuffle order. A linear head
(or a \fIhidden\fR layer) learns with the log score for \fIepochs\fR at rate \fIlr\fR. A temperature calibrates it, fitted on
\fIcalibration\fR (grammar name \[u2192] snippets kept apart from \fIsamples\fR) when given, otherwise on the \fIvalidation\fR share
of each language\(aqs snippets. The model keeps the optimizer state, so training can resume.
.RS
.PP
With \fIcheckpoint\fR, a path, the run saves its state there after every epoch (atomically), and a run that finds
the file continues after its last completed epoch, reaching the weights of an uninterrupted run. Raises
\fB\%ArgumentError\fR when the file belongs to another run (labels, featurizer, \fIhidden\fR or \fIseed\fR differ) or is already
past \fIepochs\fR.
.RE
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.error_ratio(root : Node, text : String) : Float64\fR
The share of \fItext\fR (0.0 to 1.0) that the parse under \fIroot\fR could not fit: \fB\%Node#error_bytes\fR over the text\(aqs
size.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef checked : Int32\fR
How many of the most probable languages get the parse check; 0 (the default) keeps the model\(aqs probabilities.
The check runs the installed grammars\(aq C code on the text, and some grammars\(aq external scanners can loop
forever on unexpected input, which \fB\%timeout\fR cannot interrupt; enable it only for grammars you trust.
.TP 4
\fBdef checked=(checked : Int32)\fR
How many of the most probable languages get the parse check; 0 (the default) keeps the model\(aqs probabilities.
The check runs the installed grammars\(aq C code on the text, and some grammars\(aq external scanners can loop
forever on unexpected input, which \fB\%timeout\fR cannot interrupt; enable it only for grammars you trust.
.TP 4
\fBdef detect(text : String, threshold : Float64 = @threshold) : Detection\fR
Ranks the languages for \fItext\fR: the model\(aqs probabilities, with the \fB\%checked\fR most probable reweighted by how
well their grammars parse it. Their share of the total stays the same. Languages without a loadable grammar,
and those whose parse runs past \fB\%timeout\fR, are not reweighted.
.TP 4
\fBdef labels : Array(String)\fR
The languages the detector knows, as grammar names.
.TP 4
\fBdef model : RLCD::Model\fR
The classifier: code featurizer, policy, labels and temperature.
.TP 4
\fBdef penalty : Float64\fR
How strongly parse errors count: a checked candidate\(aqs probability is multiplied by \fB\%exp(\-penalty \%* \%error_ratio)\fR
before the checked candidates share their probability again.
.TP 4
\fBdef penalty=(penalty : Float64)\fR
How strongly parse errors count: a checked candidate\(aqs probability is multiplied by \fB\%exp(\-penalty \%* \%error_ratio)\fR
before the checked candidates share their probability again.
.TP 4
\fBdef save(path : String, format : RLCD::Format = RLCD::Format.from_path(path), precision : RLCD::Precision = RLCD::Precision::F64) : Nil\fR
Saves the model to \fIpath\fR: JSON for a \fB\%.json\fR extension, binary otherwise, with weights stored at \fIprecision\fR
(binary only).
.TP 4
\fBdef threshold : Float64\fR
The probability \fB\%Detection#language\fR needs by default.
.TP 4
\fBdef threshold=(threshold : Float64)\fR
The probability \fB\%Detection#language\fR needs by default.
.TP 4
\fBdef timeout : Time::Span\fR
How long one candidate\(aqs parse check may take; a candidate whose parse runs out of time is not reweighted.
.TP 4
\fBdef timeout=(timeout : Time::Span)\fR
How long one candidate\(aqs parse check may take; a candidate whose parse runs out of time is not reweighted.
